# Line-ending rules. Paths not listed here get Git's normal text handling (core.autocrlf=true on this Windows
# machine): source code and documentation are stored with LF and checked out with the platform's line endings.

# Byte-exact data. The KU files are verified by SHA-256 over their raw bytes: at retriever start-up (corpus manifest
# hash in results/corpus_summary.json) and per file in CORPUS_MANIFEST.csv. The benchmark inputs are checked against
# their recorded hashes by tests. -text disables end-of-line conversion in both directions, overriding core.autocrlf,
# so a clone on any platform receives exactly the committed bytes. Diffs still show these files as text.
pismo_knowledge_units_migration/** -text
pismo_full_corpus_retrieval_experiment/results/** -text
pismo_full_corpus_retrieval_experiment/benchmark_inputs/** -text
pismo_full_corpus_retrieval_experiment/BENCHMARK.json -text
pismo_full_corpus_retrieval_experiment/BENCHMARK.sha256 -text
pismo_full_corpus_retrieval_experiment/CORPUS_MANIFEST.csv -text

# Shell scripts run inside the Linux PostgreSQL container: always LF, even in a Windows checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary files: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.index binary
*.bin binary
*.zip binary
*.safetensors binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
